  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying 'probable' outcomes (those above 50% probability) and averaging them. In this case, both lotteries have only one probable outcome—0 Euros—and thus the reason would treat them as equal. The individual, however, focused on the fact that the chance of getting nothing is slightly lower in A and used this as the main justification. While this involves attention to the probabilities of 0 Euro outcomes, the individual did not categorize outcomes based on a 50% threshold nor compute averages of probable outcomes. The reasoning is related to probabilities of losing, but it does not follow the specific rule of the decision reason. Therefore, the individual’s justification does not align with the decision reason’s method, even though some overlapping elements (probability of 0) are mentioned.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
